    "name": "holiday-equity-working-any-part-of-a-holiday-is-one-credit-for-that-holiday-year",
    "why": "THE COUNTING RULE, AND THE READING THAT LOOKS IDENTICAL UNTIL SOMEBODY WORKS TWO DAYS OF ONE HOLIDAY. Eid runs for three dates here and National Day for one. p-ali works two of the Eid dates and the National Day, which is TWO credits and not three; p-noor works one Eid date for one; p-zaid works a plain weekday for none. A per-DAY reading gives p-ali three and prints a number nobody could reconcile with a calendar. Two against a fewest of nought is more than one apart, so p-ali is named — which is also what makes the case assert something rather than merely fail to fire.",
